<title>JAPAN: Kumagai, Hip Hing win Hong Kong development order.</title>
<headline>Kumagai, Hip Hing win Hong Kong development order.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kumagai Gumi Co Ltd said on Thursday that it and Hip Hing Construction Ltd of Hong Kong had jointly won a 26.8 billion yen order for a development project at Kowloon Station in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>The Hip Hing-Kumagai consortium won the order from Union Charm Development Ltd of Hong Kong, which is a unit of Wing Tai Holdings Ltd of Singapore, Kumagai said in a statement.</p>
<p>The consortium will build six 42-storey condominium building housing a total of 1,350 condominiums, Kumagai said.</p>
</text>
